144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Energy efficiency is increasingly a design priority for next-generation robotic systems. Lightweight composite structures, regenerative drive systems that recover energy during deceleration, and AI-based trajectory optimisation algorithms are collectively reducing the energy footprint of robotic operations. These developments align with the broader industrial sustainability agenda and contribute to manufacturers' scope 1 and scope 2 carbon reduction commitments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Collaborative robots, designed to work in close physical proximity with human operators, represent one of the fastest-growing segments of the industrial robotics market. Unlike traditional industrial robots that require physical guarding and safety zones, cobots are equipped with force-limiting joints, proximity sensors, and advanced collision detection that allow safe human-robot collaboration on shared tasks. Leading cobot manufacturers including Universal Robots, FANUC, and KUKA project continued double-digit annual growth in cobot deployments through 2030, particularly in SME manufacturing environments.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (7.2 AI-Driven Adaptive Robots)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (The next generation of industrial robots will leverage foundation models and large-scale imitation learning to generalise across diverse manipulation tasks from minimal demonstrations. Initiatives such as Google DeepMind's RT-2 and Physical Intelligence's pi0 aim to produce general-purpose robot control policies that can be adapted to new tasks through natural language instructions, substantially lowering the programming expertise required for robot deployment.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
